comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T21:27:22.114Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for GH-911, isolated activation probes, hoisted runtime dependencies, extension install false failures, and temporary module graphs. Closed lifecycle and stale-probe items are lineage, not this dependency-topology defect. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/911"
  "2026-08-06T06:53:56.414Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: post-install and activation runtime probes now create fresh module-graph snapshots beside the active project/global topology, preserving ancestor node_modules resolution while retaining cache isolation and finally cleanup. Packed npm runtime-dependency integration, package dogfood (88 commands), manual package activation with zero snapshot residue, build, static gates, and exact full coverage pass."
  "2026-08-06T06:55:34.687Z","harness:codex","Delivery: PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/916 at exact head 0a06ef07f37d6b0b5f07d0e108d9e73b8da24910."
  "2026-08-06T07:25:40.078Z","harness:codex","Exact-head delivery evidence: PR #916 head fea4ba930cd0d1e42766510a3c4088942c2716f3 passed every hosted runner/check, including merged exact coverage, static/docstrings, Windows, compatibility, smokes, CodeQL, Trivy, TruffleHog, Semgrep, Codecov, benchmarks, and platform runtimes. Sourcery's architecture guide and Codecov/CodSpeed reports had no actionable findings and were acknowledged with contextual replies. CodeRabbit and the formal Sourcery review were rate/quota limited; each artifact was down-voted and replied to, and is recorded as a limitation rather than approval. Greptile produced no review artifact after repeated exact-head triggers."
